        "sender_full_name": "Ash Manda",
        "timestamp": 1787842723
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sounds perfect. You can mark the PR to fix <a href=\"https://github.com/gdcc/dataverse-jsf-tests/issues/1\">https://github.com/gdcc/dataverse-jsf-tests/issues/1</a> I assume.</p>",
        "id": 619568611,
        "sender_full_name": "Philip Durbin 🚀",
        "timestamp": 1787842760
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Could you re-run the tests now? Dataset actions should be more reliable now.</p>",
        "id": 619569003,
        "sender_full_name": "Ash Manda",
        "timestamp": 1787842824
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Apologies for the noise this flaky test has caused upstream. The failure in 13-dataset-actions.spec.ts only surfaces in GitHub Actions. Locally the timing and hardware is forgiving enough that it passes consistently, which made it hard to catch and diagnose earlier.</p>\n<p>The root cause seems to be a race condition: after saving metadata, the PrimeFaces DataTable AJAX cycle hadn't fully settled before we were interacting with the select-all checkbox. I've merged a PR with a fix that waits for network idle before the interaction and targets the correct inner PrimeFaces element. Should be stable going forward.</p>",
        "id": 619569552,
        "sender_full_name": "Ash Manda",
        "timestamp": 1787842933
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sure! Re-running! <a href=\"https://github.com/IQSS/dataverse/pull/12614#discussion_r3873240802\">https://github.com/IQSS/dataverse/pull/12614#discussion_r3873240802</a></p>",
        "id": 619577469,
        "sender_full_name": "Philip Durbin 🚀",
        "timestamp": 1787844652
    },
